WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.334 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-The Supreme Court

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.335 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
decided yesterday

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.771 line:92%
that Wisconsin had to go ahead

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:08.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
with their primary,
as scheduled...today.

00:00:08.742 --> 00:00:12.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, now you have a situation
that, during a pandemic,

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:13.680 line:92%
people are going in public

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've already seen photos
of long lines

00:00:15.115 --> 00:00:18.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
where, you know, people ar
exercising their right to vote

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:20.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
but also wearing masks
and trying to stay

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.089 line:92%
six feet away from other voters.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I think there's
both a core fear

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
about what that means
about today,

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.795 size:81% position:41% line:92%
but also what it means

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:31.765 line:92%
about our election in November

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:34.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can you talk about the
Supreme Court's ruling, first?

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:37.070
And then I have a follow-u
I wanna ask about November

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.740
-Yeah, well, let's talk
about the Supreme Court's ruling

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.443 line:92%
in 2013, in Shelby v. Holder

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:45.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
when they gutted
the Voting Rights Act.

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's talk
about the fallout of that,

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:51.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is that two dozen
states, almost,

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:54.854
passed laws immediately
through their state legislatures

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:59.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
that were designed
to prohibit or to interfer

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:02.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
with people's right
to exercise the right to vote.

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:05.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
In North Carolina,
a court of appeal,

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:07.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
when reviewing
that state legislature's law

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:09.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
said that the law
was designed with,

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:14.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Surgical precision to prevent
black voters from voting."

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:16.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, what we saw
in Wisconsin,

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:18.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
in terms of the
Supreme Court ruling,

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:21.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
is just more of the same,
which is a failure

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:22.715 line:92%
to appreciate the importance

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:26.119
of every person having
equal access to the polls

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:29.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
and exercising their right
in the Constitution,

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:32.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
their constitutional right
to vote.

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:34.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, what's happened
in Wisconsin,

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:39.099
God love those people
who are standing in those lines.

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:39.732 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They are committed.

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:43.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we should not make it
so difficult for people to vot

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:46.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
that only the most committed
should vote.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:47.740 size:88% position:44% line:92%
For a democracy to work,

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
it means that
everyone's voice counts

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, obviously --
-and that's not what

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:54.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sorry.
-we're doing.

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:55.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
there are a couple states

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:56.416 line:92%
that do have vote from home.

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:58.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
It seems to work pretty well
-Right.

00:01:58.184 --> 00:01:59.185 line:92%
-You know, there is this chanc

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:01.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
we don't know where
we're gonna be in November

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:03.323 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We don't know

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:07.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
how social distancing rule
will be in play then.

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:11.464
Is it important, if there'
any other stimulus voted on,

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:15.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
to start putting in language
that protects the right

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:17.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
for people to vote,
come November?

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:18.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because there's certainly
nothing we've seen

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:20.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
from this administration
that would lead you to believe

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:23.476
that they will not try to make
it harder for people to vote

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:24.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, well,
you're exactly right.

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:27.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have a bill,
along with many other senators

00:02:27.514 --> 00:02:28.548 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
a bipartisan bill,

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:31.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
to improve the elections
infrastructure of the states

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:34.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
to strengthen them
against foreign interference

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
Bipartisan support
in the United States Senate.

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:37.690
McConnell will not put it
on the floor for a vote

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:40.326
and we believe it's 'cause the
White House doesn't want it.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:44.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, we need to protect
the right for folks to vot

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:45.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
and make it
as easy as possible.

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:49.469
I believe that voting by mai
is one part of the solution.

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:51.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
We do have to deal
with the fact, though,

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:52.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
that, when you, again,
talk about race,

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:55.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
you will find that
there are certain populations,

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:57.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
in particular
African American voters,

00:02:57.911 --> 00:02:59.979 line:92%
that do not participate as muc

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:01.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
when we're talking
about vote by mail.

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:05.618
So, we have to put resources
into encouraging that to happen.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.120 line:92%
But we have got to make sure

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
that this election in November
has integrity

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:13.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that everyone, with so muc
at stake, participates

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:15.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
because the outcome
of this election

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:17.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
is gonna have
generational impact.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:20.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I wanna now move on
to lighter fare.

